# ReachInbox Scheduler requirements

# This repo is configured as an npm workspace. Install from the project root:

#

# npm install

#

# That installs the root workspace and all package dependencies for backend and frontend.

#

# Required runtime prerequisites before phase implementation:

# 1. Node.js >= 20.12

# 2. Docker Desktop / Docker Engine running

# 3. MySQL, Redis, and Elasticsearch services available via docker compose

# 4. Backend .env and frontend .env built from the example files

# 5. Google OAuth and Slack OAuth credentials if you want auth integration enabled

# 6. A JWT secret and app-level env values configured

#

# After installation and env setup, run:

# npm run docker:up

# npm run test --workspace @reachinbox/backend

#

# This file is a repo-local checklist for the install and environment setup required before continuing with the phase work.
